  "worked_solution": "Let $({x}_{m},{y}_{m})$ be the midpoint between ${{(4p,2q)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(-12p,7q)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4p+(-12p)}{2},\\frac{2q+7q}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-8p}{2},\\frac{9q}{2}) \\\\  & =(-4p,\\frac{9q}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
